**Security decisions stated for operator:**
1. Refresh token stored exclusively in `react-native-keychain` with `WHEN_UNLOCKED_THIS_DEVICE_ONLY` accessibility — never in AsyncStorage or any cleartext store
2. Android uses `BIOMETRY_CURRENT_SET` access control which maps to `setInvalidatedByBiometricEnrollment(true)` — token invalidated if biometrics change
3. Access token kept in memory only, never persisted
4. First-launch-after-install detection wipes stale Keychain data (iOS Keychain survives uninstall)
5. Token refresh endpoint is HTTPS-only; refresh token sent in request body, never in URL
6. On refresh failure with 401/403, all tokens are cleared immediately
7. Concurrent refresh attempts are deduplicated to prevent race conditions
8. The install marker in AsyncStorage contains no sensitive data — it's only an install-state flag
